# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# NOTES & TROUBLESHOOTING
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# If server shows "Standard Build" in console:
#   1. Verify you built the custom RedM binaries
#   2. Check NetworkPlayerMgr.cpp has the 0x80 pattern (not 0x20)
#   3. Ensure you're using the compiled binaries from code/bin/server/
#
# If players can't connect beyond 31:
#   1. Verify "set onesync infinity" is enabled
#   2. Check "set sv_maxclients 128" is set
#   3. Restart server completely after config changes
#
# Performance issues with many players:
#   1. Reduce onesync_distanceCullEntity (try 300.0 or 250.0)
#   2. Set onesync_population false
#   3. Enable dynamic sync distance in lxr-playerlimits config
#   4. Upgrade server hardware (16+ cores, 32+ GB RAM recommended)
#
# For support:
#   - Discord: https://discord.gg/CrKcWdfd3A
#   - GitHub: https://github.com/LXRCore/lxr-playerlimits/issues
#   - Documentation: See BUILD_INSTRUCTIONS.md, TECHNICAL.md, QUICKSTART.md
#
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
